{"body": {"model": "jev-1.14.0", "state": {"network_description": "THE OBSERVATION\nThe network sees a 10 x 10 grid. Rows are numbered 0 (top) to 9 (bottom) and columns 0 (left) to 9 (right). The outer ring of cells (row 0, row 9, column 0 and column 9) is a wall border; the playable area is the inner 8 x 8 cells (rows 1-8, columns 1-8).\nEach cell has 5 binary channels (0 or 1):\n  channel 0  agent: the cells the player controls\n  channel 1  moving objects: things other than the agent that move\n  channel 2  reward targets: things that give reward\n  channel 3  obstacles: cells the agent cannot enter or that end the episode (the wall border is always here)\n  channel 4  previous frame: the cells that were in channel 0 or channel 1 on the previous step\nThe observation is flattened to 500 numbers. Input number i = (row * 10 + column) * 5 + channel; for example input 0 is (row 0, column 0, channel 0), input 4 is (row 0, column 0, channel 4), input 5 is (row 0, column 1, channel 0) and input 499 is (row 9, column 9, channel 4).\n\nTHE ACTIONS\nThe network outputs 5 numbers (logits), one per action; the action is sampled from the softmax of these logits:\n  action 0  no-op\n  action 1  up (toward row 0)\n  action 2  down (toward row 9)\n  action 3  left (toward column 0)\n  action 4  right (toward column 9)\n\nTHE NETWORK\nA policy network (multilayer perceptron) with 500 inputs, two hidden layers of 32 units with tanh activations, and 5 outputs:\n  h1 = tanh(x @ W1 + b1)          W1: 500 x 32, b1: 32\n  h2 = tanh(h1 @ W2 + b2)         W2: 32 x 32,  b2: 32\n  logits = h2 @ W3 + b3           W3: 32 x 5,   b3: 5\nRow i of W1 holds the weights from input i to the 32 hidden units; column j of a weight matrix belongs to unit j of the next layer. 17,253 parameters in total. It was trained with reinforcement learning (PPO) to maximise the reward of a game played on this grid.", "weights": {"representation": "lossy deterministic summary of parameters, not full weights", "definitions": {"grid": "Each 10x10 grid uses original row and column coordinates 0–9. Each cell aggregates its 32 outgoing W1 weights.", "interior": "Row and column summary arrays cover indices 1–8, excluding the known border.", "output_distance": "Mean absolute difference between two W3 action columns, over all 32 hidden units; biases excluded.", "limitations": "Absolute magnitudes discard signs and hidden-unit alignment. Weight magnitude is not causal importance; biases alone are not action probabilities. No activations or forward passes are available."}, "input_channels": {"agent": {"cell_mean_absolute_weight": [[0.0496875, 0.058562499999999997, 0.030437500000000013, 0.05834375000000001, 0.039781250000000004, 0.05575, 0.0508125, 0.057499999999999996, 0.04846874999999999, 0.05003125000000001], [0.04912500000000001, 1.6072812499999998, 1.3663749999999997, 1.8290625, 1.5998750000000006, 1.6294999999999997, 0.9570624999999999, 1.05646875, 0.9370937499999997, 0.051812500000000004], [0.043437500000000004, 1.2018125, 0.0625625, 0.05803125, 1.8655, 2.21634375, 0.04981250000000001, 0.055031250000000004, 0.9300937499999999, 0.05853125000000001], [0.05334374999999998, 1.6245000000000005, 0.05525000000000001, 1.4650312499999998, 1.9822500000000003, 2.2513437499999993, 1.3555937499999997, 0.043468750000000014, 1.45259375, 0.04621875000000001], [0.050375, 2.10428125, 2.4972812500000003, 1.553875, 0.04328125000000001, 0.04890624999999999, 2.078406249999999, 1.7666562499999998, 1.4534687499999999, 0.049124999999999995], [0.04859375, 1.7042812500000002, 1.7413124999999998, 1.60525, 0.062031249999999996, 0.05387499999999999, 1.6784687500000002, 1.9495312499999995, 1.7801250000000002, 0.04603124999999998], [0.0486875, 1.10046875, 0.05975, 1.66225, 1.72921875, 1.5104374999999997, 2.0163437500000003, 0.048562500000000015, 1.4942499999999996, 0.039593750000000004], [0.042281250000000006, 1.3110625, 0.049781250000000006, 0.048031250000000004, 1.3895312500000003, 1.3471562499999998, 0.04818